<h2 class="font-headline-md text-headline-md text-primary mb-4">Common Types of Mouth Infections</h2>
</div>
<div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Dental (Odontogenic) Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial infection originating from a tooth — through decay, a cracked tooth, or failed root canal. Spreads from the tooth pulp to the root apex and can then spread into facial spaces. <a href="dental-abscess-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Dental abscess treatment</a> covers this in detail.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Periodontal (Gum) Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial infection of the supporting structures of the teeth — gums and jawbone. Ranges from gingivitis to advanced periodontitis with gum recession, bone loss, and tooth mobility. <a href="gum-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Gum infection treatment</a> covers this in depth.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Pericoronitis</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Acute infection around a partially erupted tooth — typically a lower wisdom tooth. The gum flap over the tooth traps food and bacteria, causing pain, swelling, and difficulty opening the mouth. <a href="bacterial-mouth-infection-treatment-hyderabad.php" class="text-secondary underline hover:text-primary">Bacterial mouth infection</a> has more details.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Salivary Gland Infection</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Bacterial infection of the salivary glands (parotid or submandibular) from duct obstruction or retrograde infection. Causes painful gland swelling, reduced saliva, and pus discharge. Requires antibiotics and gland massage or stone removal.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Oral Candidiasis (Thrush)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Fungal (yeast) infection of the oral mucosa — white cottage-cheese-like patches that wipe off leaving red tissue. Common in denture wearers, diabetics, and immunocompromised patients. Treated with antifungal medication.</p></div>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-8 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-surface-variant"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-4xl text-secondary mb-4 icon-fill-1">healing</span><h3 class="font-headline-sm text-xl text-primary mb-3">Herpes Simplex (Cold Sores)</h3><p class="text-on-surface-variant">Viral infection of the lips and oral mucosa caused by Herpes Simplex Virus type 1. Presents as grouped blisters on the lips that rupture into painful ulcers. Antiviral medication (acyclovir, valacyclovir) accelerates healing in primary infections.</p></div>
